<title>BOTSWANA: Botswana's Standard Chartered ups profit.</title>
<headline>Botswana's Standard Chartered ups profit.</headline>
<dateline>GABORONE 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		    (million pula unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (thebe)		    395	vs  410</p>
<p>    Div (thebe)		    48	 vs   70</p>
<p>    After tax			33.751   vs    7.676</p>
<p>    Net income		     96.263   vs   88.025</p>
<p>    Net interest income	  62.016   vs   55.925</p>
<p>    Other Operating Income     34.247   vs   32.100</p>
<p>    Bad/doubtful debt charge    3.916   vs   20.002</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			  45.049   vs    9.875</p>
<p>    Tax				11.298   vs    2.199</p>
<p>    Restructuring Costs	    nil    vs    9.000</p>
<p>Full name: Standard Chartered Bank Botswana Limited</p>
<p>Div payable on or about March 21</p>
<p>To shareholders on register March 14</p>
<p>NOTE - The bank said in a statement that 1996 had seen limited opportunities for corporate credit expansion, resulting in loans and advances declining by just over six percent on 1995 closing balances.</p>
<p>The Bank continued to be strongly capitalised with a capital adequacy ratio of 22.8 percent against the statutory 8 percent to allow it to take advantage of any large potential credit opportunities that might arise.</p>
<p>-- Gaborone newsroom +267 347182</p>
</text>
